- OVERDRAWN: emitted at the advance_day check whenever cash < 0. Transfers may take cash below 0 (no rule blocks them), and that is reported at the next advance_day.
- Storage: charged on units held before expiry that day. The same counts feed turnover.
- Expiry: a lot is discarded when `today - lot_day > shelf_life_days`. Items with shelf_life_days 0 are not perishable (C13 says ≥ 1).
- REORDER: checked on ship and on the source side of a transfer (both reduce stock). Disarmed when stock rises above reorder_level. Expiry does not trigger it.
- Transfer cost: the spec says it is a cost to the sender, but the data key is named `transfer_credit_cents_per_unit`. I followed the spec and charge the sender 25 cents per unit. Transfers are not blocked by funds.
